  </p>

  <div class="warning-box">
    <p>
      <strong>Avoid Edge-to-Edge Text:</strong> Placing text across the entire width of your canvas guarantees that words will get cut off on mobile apps. Always respect horizontal margins!
    </p>
  </div>

  <h3>Mistakes That Hurt Page Performance</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Ignoring the Mobile Viewport:</strong> Designing exclusively for desktop monitors leads to severe edge cropping on smartphones, where over 80% of Facebook browsing occurs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Overcrowding with Tiny Text:</strong> Fine print, lengthy sentences, and small disclaimers are completely unreadable on mobile screens and create visual noise.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Forgetting Profile Picture Overlap:</strong> On personal profiles, the circular profile avatar covers a portion of the lower-left area. Never position key faces or text in this quadrant.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Using Low-Resolution Stock Assets:</strong> Uploading low-resolution images produces blurry banners that damage brand trust. Always start with high-resolution source graphics.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Outdated Promotional Content:</strong> Leaving a seasonal promotion or past event banner up months after it has ended signals an inactive, neglected page.
    </li>
